     "page": 1,
     "text": "Davis-Bailey Clinic\nRe: Jacqueline Larson (DOB 04/05/1999)\n\nSeptember 22, 2025\n\nDear Underwriting Team,\n\nI am writing to provide a comprehensive medical summary of Jacqueline Larson, who was seen today for her routine follow-up regarding Colon adenocarcinoma, stage III. Ms. Larson, who is now 26 years old, was diagnosed with Colon adenocarcinoma, stage III, on June 5, 2015, and has been under my care since then. The current visit was to monitor her condition as she continues to be in a controlled state approximately 10.4 years after the completion of her initial treatment.\n\nDuring today's visit, Ms. Larson's blood pressure was recorded at 134/91 mmHg, and she weighed 114 pounds. Her physical examination was unremarkable, and she reported no new symptoms. Her overall condition is stable, and she appears to be managing well without any signs of recurrence.\n\nApril 15, 2025\n\nMs. Larson was seen today for a follow-up visit regarding her Colon adenocarcinoma, stage III. Her blood pressure was 146/93 mmHg, and she weighed 113 pounds. She has been in stable condition since her treatment, which concluded approximately 10.4 years ago. There have been no indications of recurrence, and her regular surveillance includes periodic blood work and imaging studies.\n\nNovember 06, 2024\n\nOn this visit, Ms. Larson was evaluated for her Colon adenocarcinoma, stage III. Her blood pressure was 142/90 mmHg, and she weighed 114 pounds. Ms. Larson remains in a controlled state, with no evidence of disease progression. She continues to perform well, and her follow-up appointments are scheduled to ensure continued monitoring.\n\nMay 29, 2024\n\nToday’s visit was primarily for a medication refill, although Ms. Larson's Colon adenocarcinoma, stage III, was also discussed. Her blood pressure was 143/94 mmHg, and she weighed 112 pounds. As previously noted, she over 10.4 years post-treatment and has remained in a controlled state with no signs of recurrence.\n\nDecember 21, 2023\n\nMs. Larson was seen today for a lab review. Her blood pressure was 134/93 mmHg, and she weighed 11l pounds. She continues to be in a stable condition, with no evidence of disease recurrence. The results were within normal limits, and her Colon adenocarcinoma, stage III, remains controlled.\n\nJuly 13, 2023\n\nDuring today’s visit, Ms. Larson's Colon adenocarcinoma, stage III, was reviewed. Her blood pressure was 138/94 mmHg, and she weighed 110 pounds. She is approximately 10.4 years post-treatment and continues to be in a controlled state. Her physical exam was unremarkable, and she reports no new symptoms.\n\nFebru"
    },
    {
     "page": 2,
     "text": "ary 03, 2023\n\nMs. Larson was seen today for a URI (Upper Respiratory Infection). Her blood pressure was 138/87 mmHg, and she weighed 124 pounds. She reported typical symptoms of a URI, which have since resolved. Her Colon adenocarcinoma, stage III, remains in a controlled state with no new issues.\n\nAugust 26, 2022\n\nMs. Larson was evaluated for her Colon adenocarcinoma, stage III. Her blood pressure was 140/90 mmHg, and she weighed 122 pounds. She continues to be in a controlled state with no evidence of disease progression. Her physical exam was unremarkable, and she reports no new symptoms.\n\nMarch 19, 2022\n\nToday’s visit involved a review of Ms. Larson’s Colon adenocarcinoma, stage III. Her blood pressure was 132/86 mmHg, and she weighed 120 pounds. She is approximately 10.4 years post-treatment and remains in a controlled state. There have been no indications of recurrence.\n\nSocial History\n\nMs. Larson currently smokes cigarettes, with a consumption of one per day since June 7, 2014. She is honest about her tobacco use and has not attempted to quit. Additionally, she consumes alcohol at a rate of approximately four drinks per week.\n\nPlease let me know if you require any additional information.\n\nSincerely,\n\nDr. Mark Kent\nDavis-Bailey Clinic\n"
